From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2711_defconfig: select the Victron boot logo

The kernel tree already carries a Victron-branded boot logo sized for
this exact panel (drivers/video/logo/logo_victron_800_480_clut224.ppm,
CONFIG_LOGO_VICTRON_800_480 in drivers/video/logo/Kconfig), but the
defconfig never selects it. Unlike the other CONFIG_LOGO_* options it
has no "default y", so it stays off unless explicitly enabled, and the
default CONFIG_LOGO_LINUX_CLUT224 (Tux) gets shown instead since it is
enabled by its own Kconfig default. Select the Victron logo instead and
explicitly disable the Linux one so there is no ambiguity between two
compiled-in 224-color logos.

This is a Yocto-layer patch for now; it could be folded into the
victronenergy/linux fork's defconfig directly at some point instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/bcm2711_defconfig
@@ -1095,6 +1095,8 @@
 CONFIG_LOGO=y
 # CONFIG_LOGO_LINUX_MONO is not set
 # CONFIG_LOGO_LINUX_VGA16 is not set
+# CONFIG_LOGO_LINUX_CLUT224 is not set
+CONFIG_LOGO_VICTRON_800_480=y
 CONFIG_SOUND=y
 CONFIG_SND=m
 CONFIG_SND_OSSEMUL=y
